  "upstream": [
    "CVE-2026-49975"
  ],
  "published": "2026-09-24T07:55:16Z",
  "modified": "2026-09-24T07:55:16Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: denial of service via an unbounded number of HTTP/2\n     request header lines\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-49975.patch: add the max_headers directive\n       (default 1000) and enforce it in ngx_http_process_request_headers() and\n       ngx_http_v2_state_process_header(), so a client can no longer drive\n       unbounded per-request header-list growth over HTTP/2; the counter is\n       appended to the end of struct ngx_http_request_s (not inside\n       ngx_http_headers_in_t, which is embedded by value and would shift every\n       later request field) and max_headers to the end of\n       ngx_http_core_srv_conf_t, so every existing field offset is preserved\n       and prebuilt third-party dynamic modules stay ABI-compatible\n     - CVE-2026-49975",
